1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,038
Hi, and welcome to PadDeck!

2
00:00:02,038 --> 00:00:07,703
In this short series, I'll show you how to turn an Android tablet or phone into a

3
00:00:07,703 --> 00:00:10,570
wireless Stream Deck for your Windows PC.

4
00:00:11,270 --> 00:00:13,739
A Stream Deck is a panel of buttons.

5
00:00:13,739 --> 00:00:17,991
Each button does something on your computer with a single tap,

6
00:00:17,991 --> 00:00:22,380
like muting your microphone, opening an app, or playing a sound.

7
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:29,011
With PadDeck, your tablet shows the buttons, and your PC carries out the actions.

8
00:00:29,011 --> 00:00:32,159
Watch: tapping Task Manager, YouTube Music,

9
00:00:32,159 --> 00:00:36,040
and Discord opens them on the computer straight away.

10
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:41,111
On the computer, PadDeck Desktop runs quietly in the background.

11
00:00:41,111 --> 00:00:45,960
It also includes the Stream Deck Editor, where you design every button.

12
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:51,377
You'll need a Windows 10 or 11 PC, an Android tablet or phone,

13
00:00:51,377 --> 00:00:54,877
and one Wi-Fi network that both devices share.

14
00:00:54,877 --> 00:00:57,920
There's no account, and no subscription.

